# The EKA standard declaration is a byte-pinned vendored asset: it must
# stay byte-identical to the eka-standard release asset (the embedded
# copy is the single canonical source the CLI distributes, and the
# build-time version-consistency test parses its exact bytes). Treat it
# as a binary — never end-of-line normalize it on any platform
# (Windows checkouts would otherwise rewrite LF into CRLF and break the
# byte-exact contract).
EKA -text
